# In git tree mode, bp and up start from the same tree and rewrite row 12 of
# alpha differently. bp alone rewrites row 34 and replaces rows 48-62 with a
# ten-line backport block, which covers row 55, where up changes the line
# instead. up alone creates gamma, changes notail, whose last line has no
# newline, and makes runme executable. The report must show the two row-12
# rewrites side by side and each commit's other changes on its own side, and the
# context section must show where the two results differ around the backport
# block.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: --git-tree=repo bp up
